<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KhaozEngine.MapDoc.Physics</PackageId>
    <Version>$(KhaozEngineVersion)</Version>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <Description>Physics for a native KhaozEngine.MapDoc world. MapAssetShapes reads the Collider and Selection resources of a verified MapAssetClosure as KhaozEngine.Physics shapes, refusing unreadable payloads, shapes the backend cannot install and Surface resources until R5. MapWorldBuilder builds one immutable headless world: placement geometry, interaction envelopes, terrain physics chunks with face provenance, feature query diagnostics and a build hash. MapPhysicsRegistration installs it into any IPhysicsWorld, MapWorldQueries and MapStanceCandidates answer pick, reach and walk-up stances, MapPhysicalRelations answers line of sight and clearance under a read lease, and MapResidencyOwnership and MapNavTiling name residency owners and navigation tiles. Ground support stays with the contact controller. GPU-free and backend-free: the caller picks the IPhysicsWorld. Opt-in: in NO umbrella.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- MapDoc for the document and the asset closure, Physics for the shapes and the world seam, Movement for the
         reach and ground contracts later layers compose, Locomotion for the contact shell. Nothing else: no renderer,
         no physics backend, no TileWorld.
         ArchitectureTests.MapDocPhysics_ReferencesOnlyMapDocLocomotionMovementAndPhysics pins the edges. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.MapDoc/KhaozEngine.MapDoc.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Physics/KhaozEngine.Physics.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Movement/KhaozEngine.Movement.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Locomotion/KhaozEngine.Locomotion.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.MapDoc.Physics.Tests" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
